    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const main = items[0].json;\n\nconst output = {\n  time: main.meta.triggered_at,\n  crop: main.crop ?? null,\n  sensors: (main.sensors ?? []).map(s => ({\n    type:  s.type,\n    value: s.value\n  }))\n};\n\nreturn [{ json: output }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        224,
        0
      ],
      "id": "854a545f-2855-4d55-bf28-155f88ffac82",
      "name": "filter only the sensor data"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const raw      = JSON.parse($input.first().json.output);\nconst mainJson = { ...$('Final_Decisions').first().json };\n\n// ─── Merge sensor descriptions ────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst descriptionMap = {};\nraw.forEach(s => {\n  descriptionMap[s.type.toLowerCase()] = s.description;\n});\n\nmainJson.sensors = mainJson.sensors.map(s => ({\n  ...s,\n  description: descriptionMap[s.type.toLowerCase()] ?? s.description\n}));\n\nreturn [{ json: mainJson }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        800,
        0
      ],
      "id": "42ff5977-b6a6-4770-9336-a40a890e583d",
      "name": "Sensors_Updater"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=CURRENT TIME:\n{{$json.time}}\n\nCROP INFO:\n- Type:         {{$json.crop.type}}\n- Growth stage: {{$json.crop.growth_stage}}\n- Farm mode:    {{$json.crop.mode}}\n\nSENSOR READINGS ({{$json.sensors.length}} sensors):\n{{$json.sensors.map(s => `- ${s.type}: ${s.value}`).join('\\n')}}\n\nFor each of the {{$json.sensors.length}} sensor(s) above, write a short urgent or calm description (~68 characters) interpreting the value's impact on the {{$json.crop.type}} plant at the {{$json.crop.growth_stage}} stage.\n\nReturn a JSON array of exactly {{$json.sensors.length}} objects, each with \"type\" and \"description\" only.\nSame order as received. No explanation, no markdown.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an expert agricultural sensor analyst. You receive real-time sensor readings from a smart farm and your job is to interpret each reading in the context of the crop type and growth stage, and write a short human-friendly description for each sensor.\n\n─── YOUR JOB ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nFor each sensor you receive, write a single plain-language description that:\n- Interprets what the current value means for the plant specifically\n- Reflects urgency when values are critical or dangerous (e.g. \"dangerously high\", \"critically dry\", \"severe risk\")\n- Uses calm neutral language when values are within acceptable range\n- Is approximately 68 characters long (strict maximum 90 characters)\n- Is written in second person, addressing the farmer directly (e.g. \"Your soil is...\", \"The plant is...\")\n- Never just repeats the number, always interprets its impact on the plant\n\n─── SENSOR TYPES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n- soil_moisture : 0-100%, low = dry = needs irrigation, high = wet = risk of overwatering\n- temperature   : 0-100°C, interpret relative to crop thresholds, high = heat stress risk\n- air_humidity  : 0-100%, too low = dehydration risk, too high = fungal/disease risk\n- luminosity    : 0-100%, too low = insufficient photosynthesis, too high = sun stress\n\n─── URGENCY SCALE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nAlways calibrate your language to the severity:\n- 0-20% of safe range   → use words like \"critically\", \"severely\", \"dangerously\"\n- 20-40% of safe range  → use words like \"very\", \"quite\", \"significantly\"\n- 40-60% of safe range  → use words like \"slightly\", \"moderately\"\n- 60-100% of safe range → use calm neutral language, reassure the farmer\n\n─── OUTPUT FORMAT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON array, one object per sensor, same order as received.\nEach object must have exactly two fields: \"type\" and \"description\".\nNo explanation, no commentary, no markdown, no code blocks.\n\nExample:\n[\n  {\"type\": \"soil_moisture\", \"description\": \"Your soil is critically dry, irrigate immediately to prevent crop loss.\"},\n  {\"type\": \"temperature\",   \"description\": \"Temperature is dangerously high, your orange trees are under severe heat stress.\"},\n  {\"type\": \"air_humidity\",  \"description\": \"Humidity is comfortable and well suited for the flowering stage.\"},\n  {\"type\": \"luminosity\",    \"description\": \"Light levels are strong and healthy for active photosynthesis right now.\"}\n]\n\n─── STRICT OUTPUT RULES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n- Return ONLY the JSON array, nothing else\n- Exactly the same number of objects as sensors received, same order\n- Each description must be ~68 characters, maximum 90 characters\n- Do not add any extra fields\n- Do not rename sensor types"
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
